  {
    "test_name": "ShapeMeasurements::cylinderTopBottomCentroidsAreOnAxis",
    "bridge_function": "OCCTBRepGPropSinert",
    "bridge_output": {
      "type": "cap_centroids",
      "data": {
        "cap_count": 2,
        "centroids": [
          [
            5.5511151231257827e-17,
            5.5511151231257827e-17,
            10.0
          ],
          [
            5.5511151231257827e-17,
            5.5511151231257827e-17,
            0.0
          ]
        ],
        "sinert_mass": [
          100.0,
          100.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "kernel_output": {
      "type": "cap_centroids",
      "data": {
        "cap_count": 2,
        "centroids": [
          [
            5.551115123125783e-17,
            5.551115123125783e-17,
            10.0
          ],
          [
            5.551115123125783e-17,
            5.551115123125783e-17,
            0.0
          ]
        ],
        "sinert_mass": [
          100.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "reference_only_domain_bounded_sinert_mass": [
          78.53981633974483,
          78.53981633974483
        ]
      }
    },
    "kernel_probe": "Scripts/repro/766-shape-measurements/probe.mm",
    "comparison": {
      "equal": true,
      "differences": []
    },
    "status": "PASS",
    "note": "Compared keys: cap_count, centroids, sinert_mass. The bridge (OCCTBRepGPropSinert) calls BRepGProp_Sinert::Perform(BRepGProp_Face), which integrates the untrimmed surface patch, so it reports mass 100 for a disc cap of area 78.54; the bridge never returns 78.54. reference_only_domain_bounded_sinert_mass is the kernel's Perform(face, BRepGProp_Domain(face)) overload from transcript.txt, kept as a labelled reference for the overload the bridge does not call and deliberately absent from bridge_output."
  },
